	"about_modal_title": "About JotDO",
	"about_eyebrow": "Capture fast. Get it done together.",
	"about_tagline": "less setup · more done",
	"local_first": "LOCAL-FIRST",
	"about_hero_1": "A todo appears in a second.",
	"about_hero_2": "Your team joins when needed.",
	"about_lead": "JotDO combines the simplicity of a note with the power of a shared workspace. You do not need to create a project, choose a board, or fill in a dozen fields: write down the thought and the todo is ready.",
	"about_speed_title": "Instant start",
	"about_speed_text": "Local todos work even without registration.",
	"about_access_title": "Flexible access",
	"about_access_text": "Share with a person, a group, or through an invitation.",
	"about_together_title": "Work stays together",
	"about_together_text": "People, statuses, and discussion live inside the todo.",
	"about_why": "Why we built it",
	"about_story_title": "A todo should not become work of its own",
	"about_story_1": "Most things begin as a short thought: call someone, review a mockup, buy tickets. That is why the basic action in JotDO is deliberately short: write and send.",
	"about_story_2": "A simple todo can quickly become shared. Add images, invite colleagues or family, coordinate participation, discuss details, and set a recurrence. Complexity appears only when it is actually useful.",
	"about_manual": "Quick guide",
	"about_manual_title": "From thought to result",
	"about_manual_intro": "Five steps covering the main workflow.",
	"about_step1_title": "Capture the todo",
	"about_step1_text": "Select “What needs to be done?” at the top, write the todo, and press the green arrow. You do not need an account for your first local todo.",
	"about_step2_title": "Add the details",
	"about_step2_text": "Open a todo by selecting its text. Add a description, attach images, and save changes so everything important stays together.",
	"about_step3_title": "Invite your team",
	"about_step3_text": "Open the three-dot todo menu and choose access settings. Select individual contacts or an entire group. Use Contacts in the sidebar to invite someone new.",
	"about_step4_title": "Work together",
	"about_step4_text": "A participant takes the todo into work and discusses it directly inside the open todo. You can see who joined and who finished their part.",
	"about_step5_title": "Close it and find it later",
	"about_step5_text": "When the result is ready, close the todo from its row. It moves to Closed todos and remains available through search, filters, and dates.",
	"about_tips": "Good to know",
	"about_contacts_title": "Contacts and groups",
	"about_contacts_text": "Add people to Contacts, then combine them into groups for fast shared access.",
	"about_recurring_title": "Recurring work",
	"about_recurring_text": "The repeat action creates a schedule for regular processes.",
	"about_search_title": "Nothing gets lost",
	"about_search_text": "Search finds todos while filters narrow the list by group and date.",
	"seo_title": "JotDO — fast todo list and shared task management",
	"seo_description": "JotDO is a fast online todo list, daily planner, and collaboration app. Create todos without registration, share with people and groups, discuss work, and schedule recurring tasks.",
	"seo_keywords": "fast todo, todo, todo list, task list, online tasks, daily planner, task manager, collaboration, shared tasks, team todos, no sign up todo, free todo app",
